10 times as many as the actual study. Let's also suppose that the conditional proportions
who yawned in each group were identical to the actual study. The <m>2\times 2</m> table would
therefore be:
</p>
<p>Now let's suppose that this yawning study had involved 500 people,
10 times as many as the actual study. Let's also suppose that the conditional proportions
who yawned in each group were identical to the actual study. The <m>2\times 2</m> table would
therefore be:
</p>

<activity> 
